    "code_current_through_note": "eCode360 breadcrumb 'Code 2025-05-21'. Ord. No. 973-2025 (zoning amendment, 2025-10-15) is listed under New Laws and not yet in the code.",
    "code_caution": "Ord. No. 973-2025 (adopted 2025-10-15) amends the zoning chapter and is not in the online code. It was not read. The code site's search shows it restates the IC use list with '11) Conversion apartments'. The district lot and bulk table (Table 2, Appendix A) is an attachment and was not read.",
    "checks": [
      "A 'conversion apartment' is 'a dwelling unit created within an existing single-family dwelling in accordance with all applicable requirements of this chapter' (190-202). It is a permitted principal use only in the CC Commercial Corridor and IC Industrial Commerce districts (190-405B(11), 190-406B(11))",
      "Conflicting text, ask the Zoning Officer: the multifamily dwelling definition is 'a building containing three or more dwelling units, including conversion apartments' (190-202), so it is not settled whether one apartment added to a house (two units) is a conversion apartment or must meet multifamily rules",
      "In CC a single-family detached dwelling is no longer a permitted use (repealed by Ord. No. 955 in 2022), so a house there is likely nonconforming. In IC it is permitted (190-405B(34), 190-406B(33))",
      "No standards section for conversion apartments was found. The district rules apply: CC lot 21,780 sq ft with public water and sewer (43,560 without either), at most four dwelling units per acre for multifamily. IC 'service and residential uses' 65,340 sq ft, at most four dwelling units per acre (190-405F, 190-406F)",
      "In MDR a duplex (two independent dwelling units, each with a separate entrance, the only principal building on the lot) is a permitted use on at least 2/3 acre (190-403B(6), 190-202)",
      "RR, MDR and NC do not list conversion apartments. The search found no other ADU text (accessory dwelling, accessory apartment, in-law, ECHO, granny, caretaker, accessory unit)",
      "Parking: 'Single-family dwelling 2 for each unit'. 'Multiple-family dwelling 1 1/3 spaces for each unit with 2 bedrooms or less, and 2 for each unit having more than 2 bedrooms'. Fractions round up (190-623B, C)"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Penn Township (Westmoreland County). Read on eCode360 (PE1662) in a browser, one print view at a time, on 2026-11-14. Code and New Laws search for 'accessory dwelling', 'accessory apartment', 'in-law', ECHO, granny, 'family dwelling', relative, caretaker, conversion, 'accessory unit', 'living quarters' and 'conversion apartment(s)' found the conversion apartment definition and the CC and IC listings. Use lists read for RR, MDR, NC, CC, IC and the MEO and DIO overlays (Article IV). Table 2 (Appendix A) was not opened."
  },
